  "release_evidence": {
    "qualifies": false,
    "blockers": [
      "`onnx-pyannote-wespeaker` is not in VALIDATED_PROVIDERS: ADR-0400 admits a provider only once all five conditions are met, and this document closes one of them",
      "measured on macos-arm64 only; ADR-0400 condition 1 and ADR-0081 §4 also require windows-x64",
      "inference runs in this process; ADR-0015 and VOICE_PROFILES_SPEC §8.1 require a provider that parses untrusted audio to run out of process before it ships",
      "the sessions are LibriSpeech-derived synthetic mixes, not meeting-domain audio; AMI and ICSI are the domain gate and are download-on-demand only (VP-182)",
      "ADR-0400 conditions 2 and 3 are documented for the weights in docs/licensing/third-party-register.md, but no user-facing model-pack download, licence disclosure or consent flow exists for diarization yet"
    ]
  },
  "caveats": [
    "The audio is a synthetic mix of LibriSpeech read speech: one close-talk channel, digital silence between turns and no conversational dynamics. Meeting audio is harder, so this is an upper bound on the quality of this provider in the field, not a prediction of it.",
    "DER is scored with a zero collar and overlapping speech included. Published figures that quote a 250 ms collar, or that exclude overlap, are not comparable to the `overall` figures here; the `single_speaker` half is the closer analogue.",
    "The clustering threshold is a declared default, not a value tuned on these sessions. A tuned threshold measured on the same audio it was tuned on would not be a measurement.",
    "A cluster is not an identity. These figures say nothing about who anybody is (VOICE_PROFILES_SPEC §17.6).",
    "Accuracy on read English speech by LibriSpeech readers does not transfer to other languages, accents or recording chains (VP-170)."
  ]
}
